# Converted songs staged by play.ps1. Deliberately not written next to the
# input: Commando.sng at the repo root is the byte-exact regression fixture.
build/

# Per-machine permission grants, written by Claude Code as they are approved.
# `.claude/settings.json` beside it is the shared allowlist and IS tracked:
# every rule there is one a fork would otherwise have to ask a human about,
# and a fork that has to ask is a fork nobody can leave running.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent worktrees. One checkout per concurrent agent (CLAUDE.md, "Parallel
# work"), created and pruned by the runners rather than authored. They also
# make `git status --porcelain` non-empty, which fidelity.py:3165 reads as a
# dirty tree -- so leaving them untracked stamps every generated report
# `-dirty` however clean the tracked files are.
.claude/worktrees/
# the runqueue's lock REGISTRY and its mutex are runtime state, and an
# untracked file makes every generated report stamp `-dirty`
# (fidelity.py:3165 runs `git status --porcelain -- .`)
.claude/tasks/serial.lock
.claude/tasks/serial.lock.d/

# VICE monitor output, written beside the repo when a player is traced by hand.
monlog_out.txt

# Reference material kept beside the repo rather than in it: the 6581 datasheet.
# Also, and this is why it is listed rather than left untracked: fidelity.py:3165
# stamps every generated report with `git status --porcelain -- .`, which counts
# UNTRACKED files -- so one stray file marks FIDELITY.md `-dirty` however clean
# the tracked tree is.
6581.pdf

# The graphify knowledge graph (63 MB of graph.json/graph.html/GRAPH_REPORT.md
# plus the wiki). Generated from the tree by `graphify update .`, which
# CLAUDE.md asks for after every code change -- so it is rebuilt constantly and
# would conflict on every line of every parallel branch. Listed rather than
# left untracked for the reason every entry below it is: fidelity.py:3165
# stamps each generated report with `git status --porcelain -- .`, which counts
# UNTRACKED files, so one stray path marks FIDELITY.md `-dirty` however clean
# the tracked tree is.
graphify-out/
# graphify rewrites .claude/settings.json when it installs its hook and leaves
# the previous copy beside it. Machine state, not source.
.claude/settings.json.graphify-bak

# Conversions staged beside the archive by hand while listening -- `.sng` files
# this converter produced, and the corpus copies they were made from. Both are
# OUTPUT: the `.sid` inputs the tests and the report actually use live in the
# corpus directory passed to survey.py/fidelity.py, never here. The four
# tracked entries in arkiv/ (the VB6 build, its zip, and the two reference
# .sid rips) are deliberate and unaffected -- .gitignore does not untrack what
# is already committed. `arkiv/*.sid` is NOT ignored as a class for that
# reason: two are tracked, and a blanket rule would make the next deliberate
# one need `git add -f` with nothing saying why.
arkiv/*.sng
arkiv/Hubbard_Rob/
arkiv/Zoids.sid
